  "body": "This feature request is related to [MSC3394](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/3394), and necessary for a new generation of social-media focused matrix clients like [Minestrix](https://matrix.to/#/#minestrix:carnot.cc) and [Matrix Art](https://matrix.to/#/#matrix-art:nordgedanken.dev).\r\n\r\nThese social-media-focused clients use rooms to store posts, and threads to store comments. But because of current limitations in the current permissions system, they have to choose between these two options:\r\n\r\n1. Either regular members *can* send messages to the room, and therefore everyone can write posts on your wall...\r\n2. Or they *can't*, and therefore only you can write posts on your wall, but no one can comment them.\r\n\r\nA third option is necessary, where only you can write posts on your wall, but regular members of the room can comment those posts. For that we need to have a new permission that lets someone write a message only if it's inside a thread; that is, if that message is in relation to another message.\r\n\r\nApparently this change needs to be implemented by a client before the MSC can be approved, and it needs to be included in Synapse before any clients can implement it. So there's a real need for Synapse to include it.",
